  "live_records": {
    "q-6844": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6844",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165969/assets/2c12cd35e66acc00de926a2375460242e46f359548a5112f0d87654485ba9a42.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $0.$ This occurs at the point $(-1,0).$ However note that this point is not actually included in the graph.\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $4.$ This occurs at the point $(3,4).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $0$ and $4,$ including $4$ but not including $0.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $0<y\\le 4,$ which can also be written as  $0<f(x)\\le 4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
