    "q-79265": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79265",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is the range of the function $f$ defined by the following table?\n\n| $x$ | $-9$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-3$ | $5$ | $8$ | $4$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-3$ | $4$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $f(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a table, the range consists of all numbers that feature in the row corresponding to $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-3,\\frac{3}{2},4,5,8\\}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
